    <region left="0" top="36522" width="490" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>pile stresses are evaluated considering the column actions transfer in two steps: </p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="36540" width="781" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>in the first step, the transfer of the forces Fc &amp; Fs happens in the plane π1 (Fig. 6.17) till to the orthogonal planes π2 and π3, then in the second step the transfer is inside the planes π2 and π3 till to the piles; </p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="36576" width="433" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>the truss-tie beam in Fig. 6.18 is relative to the transfer in the plane π1:</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
