    <region left="0" top="46152" width="572" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Because the condition e = -500 mm implies that the neutral axis position is lower than the one <br />previously evaluated assuming the maximal stresses for both materials, the ultimate tension <br />state corresponds to the maximal tension admitted for concrete. If we consider to change M, <br />N keeping constant the eccentricity, the tensional state change proportionally and we can state</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
